00:02:55.270 --> 00:03:00.280
The Wind, Fire and Water Above Kamogawa

00:02:57.490 --> 00:02:59.950
Sorry to keep you waiting, sir. I'm ready now!

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:01.320
Midori, taking off!

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:03.990
<i>Kyouno...</i>

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:04.950
Yes, sir!

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.950
<i>Who said we're attacking anybody?</i>

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:09.910
What do you mean? I just said it.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:14.840
<i>Listen... We can't just let you take it out for a flight whenever you feel like it.</i>

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.460
<i>Besides, how do you expect to win when you don't even have a strategy?</i>

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:19.300
The one who makes the first move wins!

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.220
That's the first rule of the Jersey Club!

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.220
<i>Get out of the cockpit and go on standby!</i>

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:23.930
<i>That's all.</i>

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:25.100
Hey, wait!

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.640
Now explain again from the beginning.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:36.270
So if we don't get rid of all three Vox units,

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.070
he'll destroy them along with Pharos?

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:40.610
His objective is pretty clear.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.910
What sort of person are we dealing with?

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:45.200
He sure is polite enough to declare war on us.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:46.870
He's debris.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:47.990
Debris?

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.450
Space trash.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.500
More accurately, he's ex-royalty from a planet

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.500
that shared a longstanding alliance with us.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.460
However, currently he's the leader of a criminal group that calls itself "Kiss".

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.130
You could say he's the enemy mastermind.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:04.260
How the mighty has fallen.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:06.140
You said we have until daybreak.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.680
According to my calculation,

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:10.850
we only have about five hours left.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:15.020
Let's say we comply with his demand and destroy all the Vox.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.650
Do you think the enemy will leave Earth peacefully?

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.070
Of course not.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:22.110
We'll just be losing our only means of defense.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:27.200
I got lost! This place is too big!

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.540
Mr. Tadokoro! You need to hear me out!

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.460
Muginami is my—!

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:36.130
All right. That's enough.

00:04:36.290 --> 00:04:37.920
"That's enough"?

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:42.880
Ms. Watabe, please find us a marine location suitable for battle.

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:46.550
We'll head there once all civilian personnel have been evacuated from this ship.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:47.930
I'm on it.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:50.850
James, report the situation to every branch of the Foundation.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.850
Coordinate with them to make absolutely sure

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:56.690
no ship or aircraft enters the airspace where the fighting will take place.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:58.520
Roger!

00:04:58.520 --> 00:04:59.570
Uehara...

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.320
Hurry and complete final checks on both Vox units

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:04.320
so that Kyouno and Laffinty can fly at any time.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.320
Roger!

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.370
Don't just stand there.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:09.660
Huh?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:10.990
It's an all-out war.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:13.700
Success!

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.040
Let's go, Lan!

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:19.790
I'm sure you understand,

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:21.170
but this doesn't mean you may attack immediately.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:23.630
Woof.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.180
I'm leaving the rest to you.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:29.970
Yes, sir!

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.530
Get revenge?

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.820
That's what Dad's email said.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.840
What's wrong?

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:08.180
No, never mind. It's nothing.

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.850
I don't get this Villagiulio guy.

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:14.970
What do you mean?

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:16.850
Why did he bother to come all the way here?

00:06:17.230 --> 00:06:20.230
Oh, now that you mention it...

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:26.820
Ta-dah!

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.070
What is that?

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.320
Let's open it and...

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.410
Find out!

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.540
Hey, what's the big idea?!

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.340
It's delicious!

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:48.470
Try it. It hits the spot!

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:50.130
I think I'll pass...

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:51.510
Then I'll try some.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:56.060
Knowing your enemy begins from stuff like this.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:08.070
Kirius!

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:11.200
It tastes pleasant and refreshing at first.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.410
But the moment it hits your stomach,

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:14.870
this overpowering sweetness hits.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.620
I was right.

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:21.620
This planet cannot be underestimated, Izo!

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.040
Man, you're so dramatic.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:25.800
It's pretty good, isn't it?

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.970
Hey, what did you go down there for, anyway?

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:33.430
Two more hours 'til dawn.

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:37.520
You'll find out then.

00:07:40.390 --> 00:07:41.270
What time is it?

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.440
Rest while you can or your body won't hold up.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:47.440
I'll be just fine!

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:50.320
My Energy is fully replenished!{The drink's name is Kamogawa Energy, btw}

00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.820
Do you think she's all right?

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:55.700
You mean Muginami?

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.080
Well, knowing her,

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.500
I'm sure she won't let something like that get to her...

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:01.660
Of course it would!

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.000
Who wouldn't?!

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:05.710
I guess you're right.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:08.050
Anyone would react that way after being told such a horrible thing.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:12.260
He didn't use to be like that.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:16.510
He was so noble, and caring.

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.470
The past doesn't matter!

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:22.180
After all, I don't know anything about that Giuvigiuvi guy's past!

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:31.650
Yes... You're right, Madoka.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:36.070
Right now, I have every reason to fight him!

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:40.120
Let's kick his butt!

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:43.330
Then... here!

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.170
Charge up and let's go!{orig: Let's go fully charged!}

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:49.460
Thank you...

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:55.590
My wife... Well, she's my ex-wife now.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:58.970
She also had quite a sharp tongue.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:01.600
She always let me have an earful.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:04.890
To be honest, it hurts even now,

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:06.900
especially when I'm feeling lonely.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:09.110
But during times like that...

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:15.070
And who might you be?

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.530
I'm from Novumundus Japan.

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:20.450
Novumundus Foundation Japan International Management Group Chief Advisor

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:20.450
Balance T. Moid

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:20.580
Novumundus Foundation Japan International Management Group Chief Advisor

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:20.580
Balance T. Moid

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:20.700
Novumundus Foundation Japan International Management Group Chief Advisor

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:20.700
Balance T. Moid

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:21.990
Novumundus Foundation Japan International Management Group Chief Advisor

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:21.990
Balance T. Moid

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:25.160
If you're here for Madoka, she already left.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.500
Actually, I have some business with this one.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:40.510
<i>Enemy unit presence confirmed. All hands to battle stations.</i>

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:41.640
<i>I repeat...</i>

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:44.770
<i>Enemy unit presence confirmed. All hands to battle stations.</i>

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.770
What is the enemy mother ship's position?

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.190
It's matching our velocity...

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.650
and hovering above satellite tracking range.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.190
Then why aren't they attacking?

00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:19.680
I thought I ordered all non-combatant personnel off this ship.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.050
Oh, don't mind us.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:23.510
I'm related to that girl.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.560
Patch me through to the two pilots.

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:32.110
<i>It's almost daybreak.</i>

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:34.110
<i>The enemy is right above us.</i>

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:39.450
<i>They're practically sitting on top of us and we can't run nor hide.</i>

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:42.620
<i>By the way, what's wrong with Laffinty?</i>

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.790
It seems she drank too much Energy.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:48.540
Aren't you supposed to dilute that stuff before drinking it?{Undeniable evidence that Villagiulio and Madoka are related. All hail our Queen!}

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:51.000
<i>I'm all right.</i>

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:54.250
I'm good to go.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:56.880
Just remember your previous battle.

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:59.090
The two of you can do this!

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.180
Attack!

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.060
<i>Opening barrier walls numbers one and two.</i>

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:09.390
<i>Pilot's heart rate, blood pressure, respiratory rate... all normal.</i>

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:10.600
<i>Opening the top hatch.</i>

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:22.780
<i>A.I. Remote Systems are normal.</i>

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.990
<i>All systems go.</i>

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:28.000
Vox Aura, Vox Lympha, take off!

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:29.500
Let's go, Midori!

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:31.170
Orca! Taking off!

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:04.660
It's not dawn yet, you two.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:13.710
<i>Madoka!</i>

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:17.460
Are you kidding me?

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:21.470
Multiple enemy Ovid launches confirmed.

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:22.880
Number count...

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:25.220
What is it?

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:38.820
The two Vox crafts are about to make contact with the enemy units!

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:40.690
Get the weapon prototypes ready for launch, now!

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:41.240
Yes, sir!

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.710
Where are Madoka and Lan?

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:56.960
They took off to get revenge for you.

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:04.260
Normally, one shouldn't sympathize with the enemy.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.590
But after hearing your story,

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:09.890
even I felt like punching that man.

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:15.810
Truly a terrible man, that Villagiulio.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:19.520
A subordinate risks her life to sneak behind enemy lines

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:22.280
and manages to steal their treasure.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:26.200
Yet he shows no remorse in discarding her, simply because she acted against his wishes.

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:31.040
Even though he was aware of your sincere feelings for him.

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.250
How ungrateful of him.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:38.670
Doesn't he realize that not everyone can achieve Memoria?

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:39.230
Hey, you have some neat stuff!

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:43.650
<i>Be careful.</i>

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:44.860
<i>Thanks!</i>

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:53.870
Man! There's no end to this!

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:56.700
<i>Help is on its way.</i>

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.000
Moid?

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:58.910
Cap!

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.210
There's someone in Ignis's cockpit!

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.130
Put it up on the monitor!

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:05.880
Her?!

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:06.960
Get her out now!

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:08.470
I can't!

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.180
She's already entered the T.O. sequence!

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:11.890
She's taking off!

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.520
Brother...

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:24.940
I'm serious!

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:29.110
If you don't stop me now...

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:31.740
This will really, really...

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:35.950
Be good-bye!

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:37.950
Muginami?

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:40.710
She doesn't know when to give up.

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:52.180
Ignis's Vox System has been activated.

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:54.850
We can no longer control it with the A.I. Remote!

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:58.470
I find her to be quite gifted, don't you agree?

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:00.770
What have you done?

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.810
You can scold me later.

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:11.740
What is it that you find so amusing?

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:18.660
Brother, if this means good-bye...

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:24.500
I might as well... I'll just...

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:27.880
Is she planning to go in alone?!

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:29.170
Muginami!

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:35.300
Let's go!

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:36.010
Right...

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:37.390
Hold it.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.640
You boys stand by here.

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:41.680
What are you talking about?

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:44.100
Are you planning to take on those three by yourself?

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:47.110
Harem night!

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:50.030
Oh wait. It's almost morning, huh?

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:04.370
It's another manned enemy craft!

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:06.630
Henceforth, it will be identified as enemy unit four!

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.960
That must be the one that appeared in Kamogawa last night.

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:15.720
Brother!

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:20.060
That bastard!

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:35.570
This is good-bye.

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:06.390
Brother...

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.850
Giuvigiubaro!

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:11.230
Madoka!

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:45.270
Stop, Madoka!

00:18:47.680 --> 00:18:50.020
<i>It's my fault for acting on my own</i>

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:53.110
<i>without ever taking Brother's feelings into account!</i>

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:55.530
<i>Brother isn't to blame!</i>

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:59.280
This is all my fault!

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:02.160
You...

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.870
stupid girl!

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:10.290
<i>Are you still defending him after what he said to you?!</i>

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:13.710
You should dump someone like him.{CHAR KICK!}

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:18.300
You have no right to say that!

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:20.630
You don't know anything about me!

00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:23.890
<i>You haven't considered my feelings in the least!</i>

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.310
<i>No one asked you to get revenge for me!</i>

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:30.980
<i>You talk big about wanting to help other people,</i>

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:33.400
<i>but the Jersey Club and everything you do...</i>

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:37.570
You're only doing it for your own selfish reasons!

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:45.660
<i>So that's how you thought of me?</i>

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:49.540
Until today...

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.250
This whole time?

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:56.420
Hey, what is that?

00:19:58.300 --> 00:19:59.800
It can't be...

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:02.300
Yes, that's it.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:21.360
Hey, what is...?

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:24.780
Madoka!

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:25.760
Is this what Villagiulio was really after?

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:27.890
Impossible! But for what purpose?

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:32.140
Or...is this just a coincidence?

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.780
The Rin-Ne has blossomed!

